:: R4-TellingJess [release4]
<<scene "img/scenes/shopping-with-jess.png" "Definitely the pink ones">>

She's home. Actually home. Sitting on the couch with her laptop, but present, here, in the apartment, existing in the same space as me. It's notable that this is notable.

//"Hey."//

//"Hey."// She looks up, smiles. It's her real smile, not the phone smile. //"DuskBlade announced the dares?"//

//"You saw?"//

//"Riley posted about it in the Discord. Well. In the community Discord. I still check sometimes."// She closes the laptop. Full attention. I haven't had her full attention in two weeks. //"So. Femboy stream."//

I wait for the cringe. The eye roll. The gentle suggestion that maybe I should just pay the five hundred because the humiliation isn't worth it.

Instead, she laughs. Not at me. With the situation. The kind of laugh that starts in the belly and catches on the way out, turning into a snort she tries to cover with her hand. Her eyes crinkle. Her nose scrunches. It's the laugh I fell in love with three years ago at a house party where she spilled beer on my shoes and then laughed exactly like this.

//"Oh my god."// She wipes her eyes. //"Oh my god, you'd actually look cute."//

//"What?"//

//"Ethan. Babe. You have a pretty face. I've always said that."//

She hasn't always said that. She said it once, two years ago, when she was drunk and tracing his jawline with her finger in bed. But the fact that she remembers saying it. The fact that she's bringing it up now. Something warm unfolds in my chest.

//"Let me help you pick the outfit."//

We sit on the couch together. She pulls up a shopping app on her phone and starts browsing with the intensity she usually reserves for Marcus's content calendar. Skirts, thigh highs, wigs, she's got opinions about everything.

//"Not the black skirt. Too goth. You want something playful, this plaid one, and these thigh highs. Definitely the pink ones."//

//"Pink?"//

//"Trust me. Pink reads cute. Black reads try hard. You want chat to think this is fun, not fetish."//

She's applying her content strategy brain to my femboy outfit. The same brain that schedules Marcus's shirtless streams and optimizes his thirst trap thumbnails is now selecting the optimal thigh high color for maximum audience engagement on my crossdressing punishment dare.

This is my life.

//"Oh, and a wig. You need the wig."// She scrolls. //"This one. Pink bob. Cheap but it'll read well on camera."//

For twenty minutes, we are a couple again. Laughing, debating hem lengths, her showing me options and me reacting and her adjusting based on my reactions. It's the most connected we've been in weeks. She's engaged. She's having fun. She's looking at me.

<<scene "img/scenes/the-phone-call.png" "Through a door that's almost closed">>

Then her phone rings.

The ringtone is different. She changed it. Marcus has his own ringtone now. A custom one. I don't recognize the song.

She looks at the screen. Looks at me. Something flickers across her face. A calculation. A weighing.

//"Sorry. One sec. Work thing."//

She takes the call in the other room. The bedroom. Our bedroom. She closes the door. Not all the way. Just enough.

I hear her voice change. It goes soft. The register drops. Her words lose their edges, become rounded, warm, a voice that curls around whatever she's saying like fingers around a wine glass. It's the phone voice. The one she used to use with me in the first months. When we'd talk for hours about nothing and everything and the nothing felt like everything because her voice was doing that.

//"Yeah, I think that's perfect."// A pause, laughter, low, private, the kind of laugh that's for one person. //"No, you're right. That angle is way better."// Another pause. //"Okay. Yeah. Tomorrow works."//

Fifteen minutes. She's in the bedroom for fifteen minutes. I sit on the couch with the shopping cart open on my phone, pink thigh highs and a plaid skirt staring back at me, listening to my girlfriend murmur to another man through a door that's almost closed.

<<set $jessMarcusBond += 5>>

She comes back, bright, slightly flushed.

//"Sorry. Marcus needed feedback on a thumbnail. Where were we? Oh, the thigh highs. Definitely the pink ones."//

She sits down close. Her thigh against mine. She smells like her perfume and something else. Not cologne. Just energy. The energy of a conversation that made her feel alive in a way this one didn't.

//"I'll order all of this tonight,"// she says. //"Should be here by Thursday. The stream is Saturday, right?"//

//"Yeah."//

//"Perfect. I'll do your makeup. I used to do theater makeup in high school, remember?"//

I didn't remember. There's a version of Jess from before me that did theater makeup and dreamed of something bigger than a cramped apartment with a part time retail job and a boyfriend who plateaued at eighty thousand followers. Marcus is showing her that version. I'm showing her a plaid skirt on a shopping app.

//"That'd be great, babe. Thanks."//

She squeezes my hand, real, present, warm.

Then she picks up her phone and starts texting. Thumbs fast. The screen tilted slightly away from me. She's still smiling.

